{title: 360 - From the Eastern Mountains}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]From [Em]the [F#dim]eastern [C]mountains [Bm]Pressing [G]on [Am]they [Bm]come,
[D]Wise men in [G]their wisdom, [Am]To [F#dim]His [Em]humble home;
[D]Stirred [G]by [Am]deep [Bm]devotion, Hasting from [Am]afar,
[C]Ever [Bm]journeying [D]onward, [Em]Guided by [Am]a [G]star.

Verse 2:
[D]There [Em]their [F#dim]Lord [G]and [C]Savior [Bm]Meek [Am]and [G]lowly,
[D]Wondrous light [G]that led [C#dim]them [Am]Onward [Em]on [D]their [Em]way,
[D]Ever [Am]now [Bm]to [D]lighten [Bm]Nations from [Am]afar,
[C]As they journey [Am]homeward [Em]By that guiding [G]star.

Verse 3:
[D]Gather [F#dim]in [G]the [C]outcasts [Bm]All [Am]who've [G]gone [Am]astray,
[D]Throw Thy radiance [G/B]o'er [C#dim]them, [Am]Guide [F#dim]them [Em]on [D]their [Em]way;
[D]Those [G]who [Am]never [D]knew [C]Thee, [Bm]Those [C]who've [Bm]wandered far,
[C]Guide them [Bm]by [Am]the [D]brightness [Em]Of Thy guiding [G]star.

Verse 4:
[D]Until [Em]every [C]nation, [Bm]Whether [G]bond [Am]or [Bm]free,
[D]'Neath Thy starlit [G/B]banner, [Am]Jesus [Em]follows thee.
[D]O'er [G]the [Am]distant [D]mountains [Bm]To [C]that [Bm]heavenly [C]home,
[C]Where no [Bm]sin [Am]nor [D]sorrow [Em]Evermore [Am]shall [G]come.
